  "notes": [
    "Tasks use their own original thresholds and rollout budgets; stabilization is excluded from the rollout budget.",
    "XMoveBendPickTeleop is a restored historical task, not an alias for BendPickTeleop.",
    "Decoupled here means GR00T Balance/Walk ONNX, not SONIC token-decoder control.",
    "Pure MuJoCo evaluation is not an official Isaac-rendered visual benchmark reproduction.",
    "Root/runner decision: retain official pure MuJoCo call and pacing semantics for initial pilots; inspect behavior separately rather than silently altering wall-clock interpolation.",
    "SonicLocoManipEnv.step calls compute_reward and then check_success, which calls compute_reward again. Contact-based rewards therefore accumulate twice per env step; do not call reward/success again in the runner.",
    "TabletopGraspMP and restored XMoveBendPickTeleop hardcode their success thresholds; do not assume assigning success_criteria changes them.",
    "Official decoupled CLI passes success_criteria=None to preserve task defaults. EvalConfig itself has other defaults, so explicit manifest values are required."
  ],
